              "text": "{\n  \"query_text\": \"According to WHO guidelines, what are the specific age-adjusted daily dietary fibre intake recommendations for children and adolescents, and what methodology and baseline adult value should countries use to adjust potassium intake recommendations for paediatric populations?\",\n  \"target_population\": [\n    \"children\",\n    \"adolescents\",\n    \"paediatric population\"\n  ],\n  \"conditions\": [\n    \"age-adjusted dietary guidance\",\n    \"daily dietary fibre intake\",\n    \"potassium intake adjustment based on energy requirements\"\n  ],\n  \"draft_rationale\": \"To answer this query, the user must combine information from both documents. From the 2023 carbohydrate guideline, they need the specific age-bracketed fibre recommendations (15 g/day for 2-5 years, 21 g/day for 6-9 years, and 25 g/day for 10+ years). From the 2012 potassium guideline, they need the methodology for adjusting paediatric potassium intake (adjusting the adult minimum of 90 mmol/day based on energy requirements relative to adults aged 20-50 years, rather than body-weight, to avoid under-estimation during rapid growth).\"\n}",
